    {
      "seq": 28,
      "kind": "submit",
      "at": 1791925254748,
      "reason": "Importing base58 used to pull in typing, a large pure-Python module, and hashlib, which loads the OpenSSL bindings. typing was only needed for annotations, and hashlib only for the two checksum functions. Annotations are now deferred with `from __future__ import annotations`, so the typing names are never evaluated. sha256 is imported inside b58encode_check and b58decode_check. Codec behaviour is unchanged and outputs are byte-identical. The work saved per process is about 42-46M instructions: decode_autofix_ir ratio 0.9593, and every other metric fell 3.3-5.0%."
    }
